          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"1-1\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_2\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The graph captures receiving, accepting/rejecting, informing, part-list handling, and preparation, but it omits the required actions to assemble the bicycle and ship it to the customer.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Early order relations are mostly preserved, but the graph imposes an unsupported sequence from reserve to back-order even though these should be alternatives, and the required continuation to later fulfillment actions is not preserved because assembly and shipping are absent.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The accept/reject choice and the parallel split between storehouse work and engineering preparation are present, but the per-item conditional handling is wrong, the required repetition for each part-list item is missing, and the accepted path terminates after synchronization instead of continuing to assembly and shipping.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"mixed_or_cascading\",\"explanation\":\"The source requires that, after acceptance, storehouse work and engineering preparation proceed in parallel; within the storehouse work, each item must be checked and then either reserved or back-ordered, repeating for every item; once both branches are complete, the bicycle must be assembled and then shipped. The generated graph preserves the initial acceptance/rejection and the high-level parallel split, but it turns reserve and back-order into a sequential path instead of a conditional alternative, omits the per-item repetition, and ends the accepted case immediately after the join. As a result, accepted orders never reach the required assembly and shipment outcome, and the item-handling logic is materially incorrect.\",\"overall_score\":0.37,\"severity\":\"major\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
